    relevanceScore: 88,
    text: "Patch 1.3. It\u0027s good. Really! The game is much closer now to what people expected at release. Yeah, they should have labeled the game early access, and no, it\u0027s still not worth full price. Base building, vehicles, portals, space stations that are no longer weird, empty shells with a single alien staring at you. All for free, too.  It\u0027s got problems, of course... survival is till tedious. The core philosophy of the game still doesn\u0027t make sense. The game demands tribute and grinding to do ANYTHING. A million players could visit a million planets and still not see 1% of the galaxy. Yet the developers insist on putting blocks to any progress and exploration. They cannot guarantee their algorithm will make every trip interesting - that\u0027s fine! Procedural at this scale is hard - so why bother? You build a warp cell to hop to a system that is a single barren planet and you have to make another.  Want to move base? Great, you lose 50% of everything you grinded for. Unless you want to dismantle everything manually and somehow find the inventory space for it all.  Even using the new portal system requires searching nooks and crannies for glyphs.  I still recommend it. When you find an amazing planet and call it home, build a cool base, find other players, it works, even without all the nonsense of \"every atom procedural\". There\u0027s an interesting idea that\u0027s marred by developers worried about players seeing too much content, for no rational reason.  Buy it cheap, slap some mods on, heck use a trainer if you have to. Light up if you want. Sean Murray\u0027s insane vision is kind of here.",
