    reviewScore: 83,
    relevanceScore: 86,
    text: "Ok, i have to update my review after NEXT.  I see a lot of flak from players, based on the old launch experience and the fact that the game will never be perfect for those people. Let me say i was one of the haters when the game came out. They lied to us! Pure and simple!  After Foundation i came back and actually enjoyed the experience. It\u0027s not perfect, of course not but that\u0027s no reason to keep hating the game. Tell me about another company that, after the bad publicity and overall bad experience that NMS had, would keep working in the game, supplying free updates for two years straight...  Let\u0027s face it people, we now have two kinds of people, those who love NMS and those who hate it, the difference is that most of the haters are still stuck in the fact that the game had a bad launch because it is, right now, on all accounts, a very good game.   After NEXT the game now has everything i wanted it to have on day one. I\u0027m not only satisfied with the outcome but also extremely impresses with the work Hello Games has done.   Do i recommend this game? Hell yeah! Do i believe it appeals to everyone? Of course not, the game is about exploration and resource management, lots of people will find it boring and repetitive.  Should you try it? Yes you should, no other game i have ever played gives me the feeling of another earth exploration and space travel as this one does. As a sci-fi fan this game just scratches the right itches.  In conclusion: Don\u0027t let the bad reviews put you off! Some of them are real but most are just people who won´t ever like the game because they feel offended by the state of it when it was launched. It\u0027s a very different game right now and i ask the haters to really try it as it is now. And if you enjoy it, like i do now, please change your review. This game no longer deserves the bad publicity it has.  Thank you Hello Games for not giving up, even after death threats, problems with justice, bad publicity, thousands of hate letters, etc etc The whole team should be proud of what was accomplished. I salute you!  *Just nominated this for \"Labor of Love\" in the 2020 sale.",
