    text: "I made a bit of a rant review with a thumbs down after the big NEXT update, because I lost all the work I had put in to the game. I was however finally after 8 hours of frustration (searching for a tiny unmarked base station) able to restore my old save game.   If I would not have been able to play from my old save then I probably would have uninstalled the game to never play it again. It sounds like I am over reacting, but the most tedius boring grind of the game is in the first 50 hours of the game. Everything is locked away in the game and they made an excessive grind for you to complete through quests and general gameplay, before you really can start having fun in the game. I simply did not and still don\u0027t want to repeat that ever again!  So now with my old stuff intact I am trying the update out for a few days and I am having fun again. I like most new stuff in the update even though it was a lot of changes to take in. In the beginning I was not a fan of the new resources refining, but it actually makes sense and it has it\u0027s benefits.  Multiplayer feature is I hope experimental, because at this point it feels very bare bones and unfinished. You don\u0027t actually meet other players in this huge universe, but they connect to you from the starting screen. It is not an MMO setup like EVE where you always have players around you on an external server, the other player is local on your connection only. And at this point I don\u0027t think you want to run in randoms anyway due to the griefing reports that are already coming in. So I have the online mode off for now till I am at a point where I can deal with those little griefers with OP weapons and stuff.  Graphics and AI have been improved alot and also the terrain is not glitchy anymore. I used to have some occasional terrain texture glitches, but it is all smooth now. The terrain also looks a bit more diverse generated, but that might be a placebo effect :)  So yeah, I am giving the game a thumb up again. You do need to expect an excessive grind in the early game stage though and bite through that before the game starts to get fun and you have more freedom in the game. And do keep a back up of your save after the innitial grind, because stuff happens when they do a big update.",
