    reviewScore: 44,
    relevanceScore: 86,
    text: "2021 update:  I would like to now say that this game is 100% worth picking up if you haven\u0027t yet. The amount of updates have added so much to the game in these past years that the game feels so full now! With the recent release of expeditions, honestly looking back at the game we had when i first wrote this review and now, i can\u0027t believe it was the same game.   If you have not tried this game yet, i cannot recommend it enough! Hello Games have done amazing work bringing this game out of the pit it was thrown into when it released and the updates are still coming out!   Ill say it again. Hello Games, Much respect and Great job!   2017 Review.  Id like to point out that i was one of the many people that pre-ordered this game and as such i have a.. unique view of this game as a whole.  This Game had a very large amount of hype at the moment of its announcement and only built up towards its release. However after release the game soon after began to receive seriously bad reviews and criticism due to its lack of content such as multiplayer and its lacklustre \"reward\" for reaching the center of the galaxy.  While it still has a lot of work to be done No Mans Sky is slowly becoming the game that we all were hyped about. The Devs at Hello Games, despite the hatred they\u0027ve received have been releasing content update after content update to give to the public the long list of undelivered content that was promised and while to my knowledge you cannot see other players yet, a vast number of other mechanics were added. From the ability to build bases that other characters can actually see and find to land based vehicles, to large cargo ships that you can purchase and use.  Last year when this game came out i would have shot No Mans Sky down in a split second. I even tried to refund it but was 30 minutes over the 2 hour limit, so it just collected dust uninstalled in my library.  Fast forward to 2017 and i can honestly say that if it is on sale it is a game worth picking up. No Mans Sky today is far more optimised, has far more content and less lies than this humble reviewer ever thought it would have in many years let alone just one! Hello Games genuinely jacked their collective socks up in a way that seriously surprised me.   Good on you Hello Games!  2021 update:  I would like to now say that this game is 100% worth picking up if you haven\u0027t yet. The amount of updates have added so much to the game in these past years that the game feels so full now! With the recent release of expeditions, honestly looking back at the game we had when i first wrote this review and now, i can\u0027t believe it was the same game.   If you have not tried this game yet, i cannot recommend it enough! Hello Games have done amazing work bringing this game out of the pit it was thrown into when it released and the updates are still coming out!   Ill say it again. Hello Games, Much respect and Great job!",
