    funny: 0,
    createdAt: '2017-08-11',
    reviewScore: 40,
    relevanceScore: 86,
    text: "Please take the time to read recent reviews, especially now that 1.3 has been released.  Hello Games has obviously disappointed quite a lot of people, and I\u0027m honestly still a little disappointed with their very limited communication with their players, but this review isn\u0027t about them and their communication skills.  I love this game. It\u0027s the sci-fi exploration game of my dreams, especially with the 1.3 update. There have been some bumps along the way, primarily one really big bump called \"release.\" This game was very bland on release, and a complete lack of communication and explanation made a lot of players angry. But this game is not the same game that got thousands of negative reviews.  Hello Games is finally delivering on promised features, and has continued to work on significant content updates(although in the dark, unfortunately). Despite the negative reviews and ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ around the botched release, they\u0027ve continued to work on this content for the players like me that still appreciated what they tried to do. Even at it\u0027s worst, No Man\u0027s Sky was a relaxing(if bland) exploration game. It was some nice, chill stress release after a long day.  They\u0027ve made significant improvements to basically every aspect of the game with 1.3. Multiplayer is slowly being phased in, even if it\u0027s still not what people were hoping for at release. The story, travel, graphics, UI, and economy and trading have received significant overhauls.   I\u0027m still waiting for 1.3 to roll out on Steam, but I urge people to give this one another shot. If you were one of the tens of thousands that had their dreams crushed when they thought they were getting an incredible and massive space exploration game and ended up with release NMS.. Give it one more chance.",
