    sentiment: 'negative',
    helpful: 5,
    funny: 3,
    createdAt: '2017-08-11',
    reviewScore: 47,
    relevanceScore: 85,
    text: "I first bought No Mans Sky on PS4 that day of launch, probably put somewhere in the region of 15-20 hours into the game, and this was at the very beginning when the content was still shallow and the community felt beaten, giving the game the infamous name of No Mans Lie. But I swear, every post launch Update has made the game better and better. 1.1 and 1.2 just added smaller new features in the game, but still new things to try out and create. But with this release of 1.3, I can happily say that the game is now great. Its got an interesting storyline with lore that I have yet to complete (its said it can go up to 30 hours worth) and the textures have been overhauled with different terrains for the planets and much more added to the game.   Yes people will be complaining \"that it should of been in the game on Day 1\" and yes I do agree. But Hello Games is learning and trying their best to make the No Mans Sky they envisioned. And you got to give the credit where the credit is due. Even look at the reviews, the Overall is mostly Negative but the Recents is Mostly Postive. That is saying something about this game which is what made me buy the game on PC to see how great it really is, since it was 60% off at the time of buying it, I am very happy with my purchase.   I just cant wait till the multiplayer is fully fledged out in the future updates, a \u0027version\u0027 of multiplayer was added into 1.3 but its nothing too fancy. And Sean murry has confirmed that its the first \"incarnation\" of No Mans Sky\u0027s multiplayer and im so excited to see whats to come.   I highly recommend this game while its on sale for 60% off as of August 15th, but even at the full price as it is on steam, it\u0027s probably worth it now.   If you\u0027re wondering when 1.4 will come out, I am too. Just be patient, 1.3 just came out. And 1.4 will probably be worth the wait.",
