    createdAt: '2017-08-11',
    reviewScore: 89,
    relevanceScore: 85,
    text: "I dont even read reviews under 3 hours and my 28 hours is not enough for a good review. So I will just say this. After I learned how to handle environment issues and inventory issues....I have had those time warp moments...8-12 hours slips by because of my enjoyment. This latest update brings the game pretty close to original goals. Wanna go and explore other planets in space? this is it. Forget the survival modes, the main game is so much better. There is space combat but that is not what this game is about Explore, scan creatures and get paid, visit space stations and set up profitable trade routes.. I whole heartedly recommend.  ps. for those achievemnt type people there are plenty and they are frequent  Edit 11/1/2021  Well I play purely hardcore now. I have quite a few more hours in the game. Now I dont know why but I have not experienced a bug in 3 years. That might be because I play gmaes really slowly and have not gotten to deeper areas were bugs may live. I did loose a couple hundred hours in a save yesterday with the coolest stuff I ever owned in the game. but that was due to a power outage when I was playing because of stormy weather, not the games fault.   I really enjoy the game play. I dont consider gathering materials a \"grind\". In fact I personally have a problem with the overuse of that word. Zoom gamers want the end game stuff instantly. Well you got to work for it. This IS NOT grind. Grind is where you play a game and have to keep repeating exactly the same area to get enough experience to handle a more difficult area of a game. This usually only applies to mmo\u0027s that do this on purpose because they  want you to spend money so you don\u0027t have to keep repeating a portion of a map. Gathering resources and building things with those resources IS NOT grind. It\u0027s playing the game.  I swear people throw around \"grind\" all the time and it does not apply. It\u0027s just something with some of today\u0027s gamers where they are filled with negativity and they throw around gaming buzzwords for the sake of being negative. Obviously I have a beef with that.   Anyway I could not even begin to list all the changes and improvements this game has made since release. But there are a ton.  But for those that dont know, you basically are \"different\" in the galaxy and you will discover what is going on because you regain consciousness and dont remember anything. Sure that has been done a thousand times but it is a great way to tell a story by discovery.   Anyway there are 2 currencies in the game. Money (credits) and tech (nanites). Nanites allow you to improve your spacesuit, starship or your trusty multi-tool which also serves as a weapon. Credits allow you to buy better multitools and ships. But not everything can be bought so your off to mine what you can find, And remember those nanites? You scan rocks, plants and animals into an electronic catalog and earn nanites for your collected intel.   There are other ways to earn nanites but since this is a discovery game I\u0027ll let you figure it out by yourself. There are a few dangerous creatures that will attack you and pirates in space also but this is more exploration than action. Well,actually pirates will try and attack you almost any time you go into space. But they start some distance from you and you are notified and can usually flee but you CAN beat them even in the first crappy ship.   BTW that brings up another irksome review snag. I see reviewers post about how bad the ship handling is in the game. That is total ignorance. Sure your first ship flies like an out of control brick (learn to make small movements and be aware there is a delay) but compare that with an s class fighter with handling improvements which come later. you can do figure 8\u0027s around asteroid groups, turn on a dime and beat 10 to 1 odds. But no! some tried the first ship one time and summarily decided all the games space combat is terrible, sheesh. These are the same people that play a hybrid action/rpg game, have a 1 out of 10 melee skill, keep missing, because, you know 1 out of 10, and report the games hit-boxes are broken. Gamer please. Sorry for the rant  Cheers.",
