    reviewScore: 71,
    relevanceScore: 85,
    text: "On release, this game was a party of letdowns, fake promises, and pissed off people. I wasn\u0027t one of those people, I didn\u0027t get a ticket on the hypetrain until only a few days before release when a friend told be about this \"space game\" that was coming out. It looked interesting, I bought it, played about 40 hours, got bored. But overall wasn\u0027t incredibly pissed off, since I still got 40 enjoyable hours out of a 60$ game. However, through the ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ that was thrown at Hello Games and specifically, Sean Murray, they continued working on the game, and providing free updates. 1.1 update Foundation, introduced base building, something I was hoping would be in the main-game. It was lackluster, however it was a free DLC to something that needed improving. 1.2 Update Pathfinder, introduced primarily Vehicles to the game. Something that made exploring planets much, MUCH more enjoyable, however I still found it hard to get my head back into the game and find motivation to keep playing.  But.  All of the sudden my friend gives me a link to a twitch stream, \"waking_titan\". I do some research and find out its an ARG for the upcoming 1.3 update. (You fed the hamster good job.) I pay a little bit attention to the ARG in the upcoming days, but the day 1.3 comes out I decide to check the reddit, I see patch notes 1.3 Hoooooooooly crap. The amount of things that have been added, fixed, improved. Is absolutely ridiculous. Lemme list some things off here. AN ACTUAL STORYLINE. And from what I\u0027ve played, its been a load of fun. Jumping to a new save file, seeing all the detail to the storytelling, and (all be it, pretty generic) quests. Is VERY enjoyable. NEW WORLD GENERATION. Amazing new biomes to be found, now also specified when scanning the planet from space. (This change is a HUGE one for how little you\u0027d imagine. Planets were usually super lackluster and boring, however now the chance of finding an amazing looking planet is much much higher, and don\u0027t even mention the new grass oooo baby) More eyecandy and things to do. Things as crashed freighters, sidequests for rewards, and the upgraded visor usability give alot more freedom in how you spend your time.  Overal, update 1.3 made a massive, MASSIVE difference to how the game feels, and makes it resemble what we saw at E3 much closer. Oh yeah, theres (very limited) multiplayer now too, a step in the right direction.  Discount price? Buy it. Full price? Think about it for a while.",
