    reviewScore: 78,
    relevanceScore: 85,
    text: "At launch this game was enough for me, it was what I wanted. Of course it wasn\u0027t what it was supposed to be. But for me, it was worth it.  After the first update, Foundation Update, the game started to feel more coherent in some areas, it was taking a direction that was what I always wanted from a game.  After 1.2, the game got even more into the way I felt perfect for me personally: Exploration.  And after 1.3, Atlas Rises, we finally got the No Man\u0027s Sky that was promised to us. We still miss some small things, but nevertheless this game took up the shape of what it was originally supposed to be, and will probably keep its way, so in few more updates, it can finally reach and be the No Man\u0027s Sky we dreamed about.  The major problem with people is: They think it was supposed to be like a CoD or Battlefield in space. That wasn\u0027t the original promise. People want to like a game that isn\u0027t for them. And then they get angry when they feel wronged... by themselves.  Today, after 1.3, No Man\u0027s Sky takes the #1 place in my personal list. 10/10 - Do recommend.  Edit - 25/07/2018:  NEXT is here. And there\u0027s so much I can\u0027t even fathom it. I\u0027m overwhelmed. You could call it No Man\u0027s Sky 2. It\u0027s so different that I barely know how to play it. I got the feeling of playing a new game. Still 10/10. Best game of my damn life.",
