    relevanceScore: 85,
    text: "I pre-ordered and put over 60 hours into the game at Launch. I enjoyed it for what it had, which was mindlessly harvesting resources and exploring. When I hit 48 slots on inventory and ship I started to lose interest simply because it was so repetative and lacked Depth. I kept watching the game when 1.1 and 1.2 came out but didn\u0027t really dive back into it yet. Not until 1.3.   I have to say..holy crap. They have flipped this game upside down and have done a fantastic job. I spent Every day this week questing and doing missions. Building bases and exploring in land vehicles. I look forward to playing it every day. If you were on the fence I highly recommend giving it a shot now. On sale or not it is finally shaping up to be what it was supposed to be. I know that it taking a year to get it right doesn\u0027t sit well with some people, but it has happened to other games and other companies (War for the Overworld comes to mind).   Again if you were on the fence before, give it a shot now. It is the perfect time to get started now that the game has an actual story to it.",
