    reviewScore: 91,
    relevanceScore: 84,
    text: "This game had me so hyped when I first heard about it, you can\u0027t believe the dissapointment I had when I saw the influx of bad reviews at launch. I decided to pass on the title for the time being, but it definitely didn\u0027t leave my mind and only left me craving the experience. Hello Games went silent after launch which did not look good for the future of the game, but it all changed when they started dropping huge content updates adding everything that was initially promised and more. Growing more intrigued with each update, the announcement of the upcoming update titled \"NEXT\" with it\u0027s fully fleshed-out multiplayer was the final straw that made me want to pick up this game, and damn was it a good idea.   I\u0027m currently only 10 hours in, but I can see where this is going and I\u0027ve got to say I LOVE this game. 18 quintillion planets to explore, probably 95% of which I\u0027ve been to so far have never been discovered by another person. The flying, the freedom of exploration, the massive universe, the art style, the music, everything about this game is beautiful. I\u0027m thoroughly impressed, can\u0027t wait for the NEXT update, and for the future of No Man\u0027s Sky.   Though incredily unlikely, I hope to see you out there in the Universe!",
