    reviewScore: 73,
    relevanceScore: 84,
    text: "Edit: I\u0027ve come around to the new update. It sucked at first, but after just a bit of re-adjusting, the true quality of this update became apparent. Yes, it\u0027ll take some time to get used to, but its well worth it. I just hope there\u0027s a greater variety of upgrades to come as i have a plethora of empty tech slots in my multi-tool and my exosuit.  [strike] 4.0 is out and I hate it. They changed how tech upgrades work and I feel like I\u0027ve been cheated out of the time I\u0027ve put into this game. I genuinely hope the technology overload mechanic is a bug in the current state as i simply cannot comprehend why\u0027d they do this. If getting ten trillion inventory slots came at the expense of the min maxing and enjoyment  involved in distributing your upgrades throughout your inventory then i want no inventory slots. I\u0027d much rather have launch day inventory size with the ability to install upgrades like old than this garbage. Seriously, why? Please tell me I\u0027m wrong and the hundreds of thousands of nanites worth of ‘archived upgrades’ I now have sitting in my inventory can be installed in a way akin to the previous version of the game, because if not then i\u0027m done. It\u0027s even worse for my ship. The thing I spent a majority of my gameplay time  hunting for is now garbage because of this. Hyperdrive range, efficiency, damage, mobility, etc, are all AT LEAST cut in half. The scrapper says it\u0027s worth over 2 billion units, but it might as well be worth 1 with all the stuff I grinded for now serving as paperweights in my inventory. I just seriously can’t wrap my stupid human brain arround this change. The people who play this game non stop have just been screwed over so that, what, people coming back have an easier time re-adjusting? Its stupid. Your most devoted fans have effectively lost more than half of their gear. I\u0027m mad and I only have 80 ish hours in the game. I can\u0027t even imagine how people with hundreds or thousands feel. [/strike]",
