    reviewScore: 79,
    relevanceScore: 84,
    text: "I\u0027ve played a fair bit of the game, and I played more than half of my 135hrs to date in 1.0, the rest in the updates. These are my short, effective points so far;  - The game was not worth its current pricetag at launch. It was poorly implemented and was missing a lot of what was promised.   - Hello Games took a LOT of vitriol for that, but they took that to heart, and kept their mouths shut, their heads down, and kept working. They did not give up on this game.  - The game has been updated repeatedly since then. Each patch has vastly improved the game and brought new content. Each initial patch has brought some level of bugs, but they get patched fairly quickly, before more content comes in.  - The game today is not even close to what it was a year ago. The game is much better, has much more to do, and is much more enjoyable.   The best advice by far for this game it to ignore the reviews, look at the bare basic decription. If that sounds appealling, give it a go. I doubt you\u0027ll regret it today, even if you did a year ago.",
