    sentiment: 'positive',
    helpful: 5,
    funny: 9,
    createdAt: '2017-08-11',
    reviewScore: 86,
    relevanceScore: 83,
    text: "Updated review as of July 24th. 2018  Is it for everyone?  No.  No game is, come on.  Did they misrepresent the game at launch?  Well, they definitely had communication issues. Have they been solidly delivering content updates and not only working toward their initial promises but also improving the game?  Yes indeed.  I am one of the few people that actually loved what we got with launch.  That said, my interest definitely dropped off after about 30 hours of play, which was still worth the cost of the game to me.  (I compare game prices to movie prices and also say to myself, \"Did this keep me $X worth of entertained?\") Update before last added quests and other features, I dig it.  I picked the game back up and played it almost the same amount that I did at launch, AND I didn\u0027t feel like my interest was dropping off any time soon. Newest update added significant new graphical update, massive improvements to how planets look, and honest to goodness MULTIPLAYER!  (if you launch in single player you still have to get to each other.  Otherwise launch in Multiplayer and join on your friends already playing.)  Buy if you enjoy: Space and planet exploration Mystery Solitude Sometimes goofy looking alien life Crafting and crafting related challenges  Do not buy if you expect: Handholding/direction on what to do.  Aside from the basics, you do not get spoon fed anything, plot your own course, pick your quests, make your own choices!  Exceptions for Expedition content. Really Good space combat.  Combat is there, and it\u0027s fun enough, but it doesn\u0027t really compare to games dedicated to it. Smooth gameplay on an old clunky PC",
