    text: "Day one player here.  I liked the game at release, and it keeps getting better.  Get it on sale, and don\u0027t look back.  The devs have added so much, and are not finished.    The most amazing part about this game is the concept of the 18 trillion planets, and the procedural generation.  The cynical may say that 2 hours in, and you\u0027ve seen everything.  I will admit that I leave a lot of planets within ten minutes, but I may be losing out.  I have hundreds of hours now, and still find novel things, and lots of awesome sights.  Then you think, once I leave, it\u0027s likely that no one will ever see this planet again.  It\u0027s kind of profound and humbly for a video game.  If this sounds cool to you, it\u0027s worth the $60.  It\u0027s definitely worth $25.  Compared to discovering a unique universe, what\u0027s a couple of bucks?",
