    relevanceScore: 83,
    text: "I love open-ended exploration games, and space games, and sci-fi games, so after watching No Man\u0027s Sky for a long time I finally dove in after the latest updates and an upswing in positive reactions. What a disappointment. There is no feeling of exploration because the universe is so homogenous. Yeah, I can fly to the next planet over there and the one after that, but why bother? Every planet is almost, but not entirely quite like all the other ones you\u0027ve been on. This would be ok if the mechanics are interesting, but they\u0027re not. Boring. Repetitive. Pointless. No feeling of exploration or purpose. I expected it to grow on me, and tried really hard to allow it to, but in the end it was just a waste of time and money.",
