    text: "Pick the game up on sale. They\u0027ve added a lot of content to the game, and while it\u0027s still not anything like what was advertised (let\u0027s be honest, that advertising was just insane. overhyping trash for a game that had like 10% of what was promised, at 60$) It still manages to be a great game. I\u0027d recommend this game if you are mainly into adventuring around in games, as it does a great job at providing a very relaxing exploration experience. They\u0027ve added much more to the game such as base building but for me the main draw that got me to reinstall the game and give it another shot was the addition of freighters. They basically act as a way around the ♥♥♥♥♥♥ inventory system, which also I might add feels a lot more improved than when the game first launched  Overall, definitly give it a chance. It\u0027s nothing like what was advertised, as they set peoples expectations way too high. But, if you are going to buy it, I would definitly wait till it is on sale as 60$ is way too steep for what is offered.  Hopefully the addition of multiplayer will improve the game even more but still, I don\u0027t see it being worth that much",
