    createdAt: '2017-08-11',
    reviewScore: 71,
    relevanceScore: 81,
    text: "Like a lot of people on here I bought the game at release and was very disappointed with what was presented.  While the game quality has certainly increased and there are a lot more things to do, there is still room for more content (namely an imrovement on animal AI) but by the looks of it Hello Games has really been working hard to create a polished, fun game.  It`s too bad I spent the full $60 at release and had to wait many months for any considerable work to be done, but better late than never I guess.  The game certainly felt like it was early access or something when it first released, which put off a lot of people as it was marketed as a full blown title, so long as these free updates keep coming though I can overlook what was in the past, it was probably Sony who made them put it out in the original state anyhow.  While the price tag is still a bit steep for my liking for what the game offers, it definitely looks like it will be the game promised at launch over the next few updates.  I think once full blown multiplayer and co-op is established, and the animals (oh, those animals) get an AI overhaul the game will certainly be worth the $60+.    In conclusion, while the game has made an amazing recovery from the initial backlash it got on release, there are still some patches needed to really flesh it out as the game Hello Games wanted, but I am quite optimistic at this point which is great because it was hard to find optimism for this game several months ago.  Yes I recommend, but if you`re uncertain I`d say wait for a few more patches if you really want bang for your buck.",
