    text: "- Recent updates have definitely improved the experience of No Man\u0027s Sky. - New UI update looks MUCH better and feels well organised, with an in-depth and useful Guide for tutorials, tips and notes. - I already found exploring, tavelling and crafting fun in this game, and levelling up gear and collecting the right resources to craft a new piece of equipment etc is rewarding. - Reaching milestones is very rewarding, especially when it appears on screen - there\u0027s just something pleasing about being notified of your progress like this. - Again, the UI looks SO MUCH BETTER, from menus, to the options and text that appear when speaking to an alien. The addition of the Mission Board is a HUGE improvement.  To keep this short, they have improved this game a lot since I initially purchased it (and since the initial controversy) and I personally find it enjoyable to play and progress.   I feel that initial players should return to the game to experience its improvements, and that new players shouldn\u0027t fear it\u0027s tainted reputation but give it a chance. However, I do feel the price should be dropped due to its shaky start when it first came out, but if this game appears in sales or as a deal, I would recommend it.",
