    reviewScore: 53,
    relevanceScore: 81,
    text: "There are some positives.   It was enjoyable for about 300 hours of game play.  After exploring about 7 solar systems, you realize there are only about a dozen different planet types, about 14 different creatures and about 20 different flora, and everything else is a randomly generated variant on those basics.  The main quests don\u0027t pay off very well, and the side quests are very limited and monotonous.  Each planet has the same half a dozen types of things to find, and you quickly max out your ship, suit and weapon and then it becomes pointless.  It is nicely seamless, but a bit buggy (ie, right now my base has grass suddenly growing up through the floor and although it is on a \"paradise\" planet, suddenly I have toxic rain?).  From what I understand some of the upgrades like Atlas and Pathfinder improved it...can\u0027t imagine what it was like before them.  If they would keep adding planet/flora/fauna/ship/weapon/etc. types and add cities and civilizations (even abandoned ones) it would keep me going on it, but at the moment, I\u0027m done.  If that kind of time is all you want, its fine, but being billed as a limitless game with a quintillion different planets is kind of a half truth.",
