    sentiment: 'negative',
    helpful: 3,
    funny: 3,
    createdAt: '2017-08-11',
    reviewScore: 37,
    relevanceScore: 80,
    text: "I have been playing No Man\u0027s Sky since it\u0027s release day on PS4. I eventually switched to PC after the first or second major update and haven\u0027t regretted it.  Honestly, if you don\u0027t mind a relaxing, do almost whatever you want kind of space exploring game, then why the hell are you even here?  This game is just a nice space exploration game with some story elements thrown in to keep you going. However, that doesn\u0027t mean it\u0027s bad. Oh no, on the contrary in fact...  This game is everything I could ask for in a space game. -Ships -Goals -Randomized planets -Randomized animals -Randomized EVERYTHING -New gear to aquire -A story line that doesn\u0027t force you to follow it -Base building -Ship collecting -Challenges (when sought after)  I honestly love this game and have since launch day. The reason for that is because I wasn\u0027t hyped for some overblown multiplayer space extravaganza... No, I was expecting a space game with exploration in mind and a really, really good soundtrack. Something I could come home to and relax with from a long day at work.  This game is everything I could of asked for, and now, with all the free content updates is even more than I could of ever wanted.  Keep up the good work Sean and Team at Hello Games. I salute you. *Salute*",
