    reviewScore: 57,
    relevanceScore: 80,
    text: "Look here I\u0027m just going to give it to you STRAIGHT UP. When I bought this game in November I was PLEASED. Now for months the exploration was fun, but I\u0027d find myself slightly wanting something else to do.  I started getting slightly bored due to it feeling lonely and empty and MINECRAFT gave me this exact same feeling. It seems like something happened before launch that caused the game to feel like early access, like they had a forced deadline or something at sony and still had to push the game???  (Thats the only thing that seems logical for having items without any use or functioning code behind them or unless they built the game to expand over the seasons???)   Then comes the foundation UPDATE that adds more to DO! It FED my want for more so from there I was pleased to a certain point then here comes the PATHFINDER UPDATE and I am thourougly pleased, it started opening a pathway to do MORE. I played for over 6 hours and I NEVER play games for THAT long because my attention span is horrible, but this,.......... this  game has truly capsulated what it means to have fun exploring a universe.  Now here we are at the ATLAS RISES UPDATE(v1.3) and I am blown away  ✔we have missions ✔we have a thourough storyline ✔we have basic multiplayer(*joint exploration*which is step A out of many to go) ✔we have animals from E3 ✔we have portals  ✔we have a purpose  Im 100% recommending this game ESPECIALLY while its on SALE.",
